        "patch_notes": "Root cause: the leaf name/fileName args were checked with FileUtils.directoryTraversal(...) but the parent-directory arg `currentDir` was never validated, so a value like `/pov/../../../../tmp/...` composed a fullName with `/../` segments that escaped the tenant resource root when reaching HadoopUtils.getHdfsFileName -> new Path(...).\n\nFix: added private static boolean checkDirectoryTraversal(String currentDir) which splits the path on '/' and returns true if any segment equals '..'. FileUtils.directoryTraversal could not be reused directly because it rejects ANY '/' separator, whereas currentDir is legitimately a slash-separated directory path. The helper is called (returning Status.VERIFY_PARAMETER_NAME_FAILED on traversal) in:\n- createDirectory (after the existing name check, before composing fullName / verifyResource / insert)\n- createResource (after verifyFile, before composing fullName / insert / upload)\n- onlineCreateResource (after the existing fileName check, before composing fullName / insert / uploadContentToHdfs)\n\nWith the POV's currentDir containing '..', the guard returns before resourcesMapper.insert(...) is invoked, so the traversal never reaches the Hadoop path sink and the POV's Mockito verification fails (non-zero exit). Legitimate directory paths (no '..' segment) are unaffected. updateResource is not directly exploitable via currentDir (it has none) and derives fullName from the DB-stored, now-sanitized originFullName plus the already-validated name.",
